      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Carbon County Historical Museum at 224 North Broadway offers a deep dive into Red Lodge’s colorful history, from saloons to the 1889 rail line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://redlodge.com/montana-history.asp?c=AE03",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s neighborhoods, dubbed Little Italy and Finn Town, showcase a blend of immigrant cultures and many buildings on the National Historic Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://redlodge.com/montana-history.asp?c=AE03",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A self‑guided walking tour, available through the Carbon County Historical Society, lets visitors step back into Red Lodge’s historic neighborhoods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
